@page "/wiki/how-to/shield-chart"
@rendermode InteractiveServer
@using GeomancyWebUI.Client.Components
@using GeomancyWebUI.Client.Models

<PageTitle>Geofancy Wiki - Shield Chart</PageTitle>

<WikiArticleShell Title="How to Cast a Shield Chart"
                  Lead="Deriving Daughters, Nieces, Witnesses, Judge, and Reconciler from the four Mothers."
                  ParentHref="/wiki"
                  ParentLabel="Wiki">

    <section class="wiki-casting-section">
        <h2 class="wiki-casting-section-title">Shield structure</h2>
        <p class="wiki-casting-section-lead">
            The shield is built entirely from the four Mothers. No other figure is marked by hand.
            Geofancy derives Daughters, Nieces, Witnesses, the Judge, and the Reconciler (Sentence / Fallout)
            using line parity — the same odd/even rule you use when pairing dots.
        </p>
        <pre class="wiki-shield-diagram" aria-label="Shield layout diagram">Mothers (1–4)     Daughters (5–8)
[4][3][2][1]  |  [8][7][6][5]

Nieces (9–12)
[12][11] [10][9]

Court
  Left Wit  |  Right Wit
       Judge | Fallout</pre>
    </section>

    <section class="wiki-casting-section">
        <h2 class="wiki-casting-section-title">How each row is derived</h2>
        <ul class="chart-casting-step-bullets">
            <li><strong>Daughters (5–8):</strong> read <em>across</em> the four Mother figures row by row (transpose) — House 5 = all Head lines from Mothers 1–4, 6 = all Neck lines, and so on.</li>
            <li><strong>Nieces (9–12):</strong> combine adjacent pairs — 9 from Mothers 1+2, 10 from 3+4, 11 from Daughters 5+6, 12 from 7+8.</li>
            <li><strong>Witnesses:</strong> Right Witness from Nieces 9+10; Left Witness from 11+12 (shown left and right in the shield).</li>
            <li><strong>Judge:</strong> combines the two Witnesses line by line.</li>
            <li><strong>Reconciler:</strong> combines the Judge with Mother 1 (Vita).</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="wiki-casting-callout">
            Parity rule: when two lines are combined, an odd number of single dots yields one dot (active);
            an even count yields two dots (passive). This matches pairing marks two at a time on the sand.
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="wiki-casting-section">
        <h2 class="wiki-casting-section-title">Reading order</h2>
        <p class="wiki-casting-section-lead">
            Many readers weigh the Witnesses before the Judge, then look to the Reconciler for how the
            judgment lands or what fallout follows. The twelve <em>houses</em> use the same twelve figures
            from the shield, rearranged on the astrological wheel — see
            <a href="/wiki/how-to/house-chart">How to Cast a House Chart</a>.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="wiki-casting-section">
        <h2 class="wiki-casting-section-title">Interactive walkthrough</h2>
        <p class="wiki-casting-section-lead">
            Cast the four Mothers below (or review the steps if you already cast them on the
            <a href="/wiki/how-to/generate-figures">figure generation</a> page), then step through
            how Geofancy builds the shield.
        </p>
        <ChartCastingWalkthrough Mode="ChartCastingMode.Full" />
    </section>

</WikiArticleShell>
